    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (**55 tests, 0 failures**). Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Request/response contract** (`openapi.yml`)\n- Added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` fields to the `OwnerFields` schema.\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list (and its `minLength: 1`), so the flat form is no longer mandatory \u2014 an owner may now supply an address in either the structured or flat form. Documented `address` as the composed, normalized value on read.\n\n**Domain model** (`Owner.java`)\n- Added persisted `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` columns with getters/setters so they survive a create\u2192GET round-trip.\n- Added `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns to all four DB schemas (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres).\n\n**Address normalization & composition** (`OwnerAddresses.java`)\n- Added `applyTo(request)`: normalizes whichever address fields are supplied, and composes the stored/returned flat `address`. Structured is preferred \u2014 when `addressLine1` is non-blank the address becomes the normalized `addressLine1`, with a single space plus normalized `addressLine2` appended when present; otherwise the normalized flat `address` is kept (backward-compatible).\n\n**Pipeline wiring**\n- `ValidateOwnerFields` (create) now calls `applyTo`, so validity requires an address in *either* form plus city.\n- `ApplyOwner` (update) applies the same normalization/composition for consistency.\n\n**Postcode validation fix** (`ValidateOwnerPostcode.java`)\n- A new test (Cp29) requires a postcode to be validated against the **city's** region (Sydney\u2192NSW rejects 3000). The function previously used `getLocality()`, which prefers the postcode itself and would wrongly accept 3000 for Sydney. Switched it to resolve the region from the city \u2014 matching the function's own documented intent \u2014 with a null-safe guard (`Map.of(...).get(null)` throws NPE), which cities outside the known table now sidestep.\n\nEverything that reads the address (household hash, postcode validation, locality) works off the structured `postcode`/`city` fields that now flow through unchanged for structured owners.",
